Default 3’s `median —` is honest, and omitting Done/Halted medians is appropriate for this handoff-based measure; those omissions are established by the prototype, since those columns are outside the supplied captures.
Default 4 needs meaningful policy copy, while Default 5’s local select and unchanged totals are appropriate.
The three-line column headers remain readable at 1280, 640 and 390; the taller phone stack is acceptable, and DIRECTION’s agent-written two-line prescription should not force compression.
The architect can resolve the two blockers through copy and policy-description changes within the existing layout.
